== (6) what 'confidence 1 - delta' means for the certificate of 13.1(a1) ==
   m = 100, delta = 0.05: the certificate claims rho <= 0.0300.
   an imitator with rho = 0.0150: certificate issued with probability 0.2211; the claim is true
   an imitator with rho = 0.0300: certificate issued with probability 0.0478; the claim is true
   an imitator with rho = 0.0303: certificate issued with probability 0.0463; the claim is FALSE
   an imitator with rho = 0.0599: certificate issued with probability 0.0021; the claim is FALSE
   an imitator with rho = 0.1498: certificate issued with probability 0.0000; the claim is FALSE
   If the imitators submitted to validation all have rho = 1.01 * thr, every issued certificate is false,
   although each is issued with probability < delta.  So 'whenever it is issued it is false with probability
   less than delta' (Corollary 13.2) must read 'a false certificate is issued with probability less than delta'.

